        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanity test_56wa",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanity test_56wa\n\ntest_56wa creates 200 hard links to dir1/file1 and then pipes\nlfs find into lfs migrate, which migrates the same file once per\nlink. The 200 links date from LU-6051, when the old lfs_migrate\nscript deduplicated hard links, and no longer check anything\nspecific. test_56xb still covers lfs_migrate with many links.\n\nCreate 2 links instead, which still exercises migrating a\nhard-linked file. Drop the MDS 2.5.55 version check around the\nlinks, since no server that old can interoperate, and fix the\nstale comment there.\n\nIn three runs each on a VM, the test took 5 to 7s instead of\n36 to 43s. At 17047 CI runs per 30 days that saves about 30s\nper run, over 140 hours; CI runs take far longer than the VM\n(mean 194s), so the saving there should be larger.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=56wa\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I589d0d9f52161d9c0532a3601e56fdf75238d999\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
